From fb1686e2a753c164da9c432a0d3c52f6defe70a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:18:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/53] Route OBS's own Start/Stop Streaming through the
 LiveHime session

Add obs_frontend_set_start_streaming_override(): a plugin may take over
user-initiated Start Streaming (controls button, hotkeys, tray, frontend
API). OBSBasic::StartStreaming consults it before setting up the output.

With a ready Bilibili account the LiveHime plugin turns OBS's Start into
Go live, so the stream always uses the room's current endpoint; signed
out, OBS streams with the user's own settings. Starts issued by the
plugin itself pass through. Stopping a Go live stream from OBS's own
controls now also closes the Bilibili room, as End live does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
